1
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:04,571
Every school should observe lessons.

2
00:00:04,571 --> 00:00:07,884
Very few can show what happens next.

3
00:00:07,884 --> 00:00:19,481
This is the Observation System: one route from lesson observation, to collected evidence, to a coaching plan for every teacher, covering every step of the learning journey.

4
00:00:21,481 --> 00:00:22,215
Step one.

5
00:00:22,215 --> 00:00:25,150
The teachers are observed by their coach.

6
00:00:25,601 --> 00:00:40,236
While the coaches are observing a lesson, they fill in the relevant observation form: subject, class and teacher, with live dropdowns fed by the school's own staff directory, so nothing is typed from memory and no list is ever out of date.

7
00:00:40,236 --> 00:00:42,675
Class composition is a few taps.

8
00:00:42,675 --> 00:00:46,508
The whole context of the lesson, captured throughout the observation.

9
00:00:46,957 --> 00:00:55,525
Each observation uses the Regulatory Body's own six point scale, from Very Weak to Outstanding, with the same proportion bands its inspectors already use.

10
00:00:55,525 --> 00:01:01,593
Ten criteria, from attainment and progress to teaching and leadership, each with room for a comment.

11
00:01:01,593 --> 00:01:08,376
The form speaks the language of inspection, because it was built to coach teachers using the same criteria.

12
00:01:08,826 --> 00:01:17,110
The coach fills in the form by typing their notes, or by writing them with the Apple Pencil on the built in Evidence Pad.

13
00:01:17,110 --> 00:01:23,323
The Evidence Pad also lets the coach take or attach photos of anything noteworthy in the lesson.

14
00:01:23,323 --> 00:01:27,120
The system transcribes the handwriting and turns it into text.

15
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:32,298
Everything is saved automatically throughout the observation, so nothing is ever lost mid lesson.

16
00:01:32,748 --> 00:01:36,155
When it is done, each observation gets its own ID.

17
00:01:36,155 --> 00:01:38,881
Everything is saved, and ready for review.

18
00:01:39,331 --> 00:01:41,990
One tap files everything, four ways at once.

19
00:01:41,990 --> 00:01:44,316
The observation lands in a spreadsheet.

20
00:01:44,316 --> 00:01:47,972
It mirrors into a live database, duplicate proof by design.

21
00:01:47,972 --> 00:01:56,281
After each coaching observation, an email is sent to the observer, for safe keeping and immediate easy access, with a link to the observation.

22
00:01:56,281 --> 00:02:04,590
Even the form's Evidence Pad handwriting, and any attached pictures, are archived in secured storage, so everything can be fully reviewed if ever needed.

23
00:02:07,589 --> 00:02:08,423
Step two.

24
00:02:08,423 --> 00:02:11,344
Retrieving and viewing the collected evidence.

25
00:02:11,794 --> 00:02:15,820
For example: first, we open the Observation Dashboard, which is password protected.

26
00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:19,845
Here is an observation round from one of the associated schools.

27
00:02:19,845 --> 00:02:26,890
The story plays itself: a hundred and eleven lessons, a hundred and five teachers, counted up live from the data.

28
00:02:26,890 --> 00:02:29,909
Where judgements sit on the six point scale.

29
00:02:29,909 --> 00:02:31,251
What is working.

30
00:02:31,251 --> 00:02:32,928
Where to focus next.

31
00:02:32,928 --> 00:02:39,973
And one tap presents that round's findings in full screen, built to showcase the round by itself in any meeting.

32
00:02:40,424 --> 00:02:45,685
Once an observation round is completed, the relevant school stakeholders receive a whole set of data.

33
00:02:45,685 --> 00:02:46,1000
Individual lesson observations.

34
00:02:46,1000 --> 00:02:48,973
A snapshot of the round.

35
00:02:48,973 --> 00:02:49,630
Coverage.

36
00:02:49,630 --> 00:02:51,603
And a highly detailed report.

37
00:02:52,052 --> 00:02:54,740
Rounds can be compared to show teacher progression.

38
00:02:54,740 --> 00:03:04,819
Every teacher seen in both rounds is displayed from one judgement point to the next, from where they were to where they are, green when they moved toward Outstanding.

39
00:03:04,819 --> 00:03:08,851
A transition matrix counts the improvements, the holds and the declines.

40
00:03:08,851 --> 00:03:12,883
This is the question governors actually ask: is teaching getting better?

41
00:03:12,883 --> 00:03:14,227
If not, why?

42
00:03:14,227 --> 00:03:16,243
And how can we improve?

43
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:24,942
The report is generated using citations and references from the actual observations.

44
00:03:24,942 --> 00:03:32,919
Every written statement carries a small number: a citation count, showing how many times that statement is cited across the lesson observations.

45
00:03:32,919 --> 00:03:41,937
Click or tap the number to open the citations and see the actual observations behind each statement: subject, date, judgement, and the inspector's words, verbatim.

46
00:03:41,937 --> 00:03:46,446
AI cites the hundreds of references that sit behind every claimed statement.

47
00:03:46,446 --> 00:03:55,464
Nothing on this dashboard is an opinion without evidence, and it can all be presented to your regulatory body at the click of a button.

48
00:03:16,693 --> 00:03:18,651
This is where the real magic happens.

49
00:03:18,651 --> 00:03:20,330
With the help of AI.

50
00:03:55,914 --> 00:04:01,697
For the leadership table, one button turns the round into a governance report, simple or in depth.

51
00:04:01,697 --> 00:04:08,841
One tap or click, and you have a PDF or a Google Doc, all references attached, teachers anonymised by construction.

52
00:04:08,841 --> 00:04:18,366
When a new round lands, one more button rewrites the analysis for it, the AI's work double checked by the Head of Teaching and Learning before publishing.

53
00:04:18,816 --> 00:04:23,692
The Dashboard also shows Coverage, which answers the other question: who has been seen?

54
00:04:23,692 --> 00:04:31,702
Teachers on the register, teachers observed, lessons per teacher, and who is still waiting, so no one is invisible for a term.

55
00:04:34,202 --> 00:04:34,942
Step three.

56
00:04:34,942 --> 00:04:36,421
The coaching plan.

57
00:04:36,871 --> 00:04:39,601
Drill into any teacher and their history follows.

58
00:04:39,601 --> 00:04:43,356
Two gauges, student progress and teaching, averaged across every observation.

59
00:04:43,356 --> 00:04:47,110
Each session, its skills and its notes, one card each.

60
00:04:47,110 --> 00:04:59,739
And below them, a coaching plan: drafted by AI from that teacher's own lessons, checked word for word against the observed lesson itself, grounded in the school's own rubric and its strategic plan, aiming for excellence.

61
00:04:59,739 --> 00:05:04,859
The coach reads it, edits and amends it if needed, then approves the plan.

62
00:05:04,859 --> 00:05:07,589
Once approved, the teacher can review it.

63
00:05:08,039 --> 00:05:09,571
Teachers have their own door.

64
00:05:09,571 --> 00:05:16,311
A portal for every member of staff: their photograph, their history, and a notification when a new coaching plan is approved.

65
00:05:16,311 --> 00:05:19,681
What they see is deliberately thinner than what leadership sees.

66
00:05:19,681 --> 00:05:26,115
No observer's rough notes, no edits, no other teachers, only their own approved coaching plan and their own next steps.

67
00:05:26,565 --> 00:05:31,305
From a lesson observed, to evidence, to a coaching plan in the teacher's hand.

68
00:05:31,305 --> 00:05:36,045
And when the next round begins, the journey starts again: observe, evidence, coach.

69
00:05:36,045 --> 00:05:37,399
Better never stops.
